import java.util.* ;
import java.io.*; 
import java.util.ArrayList;

public class Solution {

	public static ArrayList<ArrayList<Integer>> numberPattern(int n) {

		// Write your code here.
		ArrayList<ArrayList<Integer>> ans = new ArrayList<>();
		int num = 1;
		for(int i = 1; i <= n; i++){
			ArrayList<Integer> list = new ArrayList<>();

			for(int j = 1; j <= n-i; j++){
				list.add(-1);
			}

			for(int k = 1; k <= i; k++){
				list.add(num);
				num++;

				if(num > 9) num = 1;
			}
			ans.add(list);
		}
		return ans;
	}
}



Ninja wants to create a right-aligned triangle of numbers across N rows. The first row contains 1 number, the second contains 2, and so on. 
The numbers increase sequentially starting from 1 and wrap back to 1 after 9.

You are given an integer ‘N’ denoting the given number of rows. Can you print the pattern that Ninja wants to create?

